window.docContents[224].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.LibsignalE2E.StateXModel/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___LibsignalE2E___StateXModel":{"contents":"Paper › LibsignalBinary/Specifications/LibsignalE2E › StateXModel.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof 3 headline theorems depend on it 58 of 105 lines trusted trust banner B2, trusted: definitions used by the statement source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nDeclarations on this page (9)structure RecordExtrasdef uint64FieldXdef int32FieldXdef optUint32FieldXdef encPendingPreKeyXdef encPendingKyberXdef encStateUnderExtrasdef encodeRecordUnderExtrasdef binStateOfUnderExtras\n\nSession-Record Encoding with PQXDH Extras (encodeRecordUnderExtras)Trusted: definitions used by the statement. Generalizes encodeRecord (State.lean, DEV-M9) from constant placeholder fields to the per-session public transcript fields RecordExtras produced by a PQXDH handshake (pending_pre_key, pending_kyber_pre_key with Kyber1024 round-3 ciphertext per DEV-PQ2, registration IDs, and alice_base_key). Both pending sub-messages are emitted iff st.pendingPreKey holds. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.\n\n\n\nThe record extras\n\nstructure RecordExtrasL34–48 ↗#The SessionStructure fields of one party's record that the session model does not track, constant over one session: the pending pre-key and pending Kyber pre-key (written only while the session model's pendingPreKey flag is set), the registration ids and alice_base_key. Field numbers: libsignal v0.105.4 rust/protocol/src/proto/storage.proto.\n\nField writers not needed by State.lean\n\ndef uint64FieldXL52–54 ↗#proto3 uint64: omitted when 0.\n\ndef int32FieldXL56–58 ↗#proto3 int32: omitted when 0; a negative value is sign-extended to 64 bits (prost).\n\ndef optUint32FieldXL60–63 ↗#optional uint32 (explicit presence): written whenever some.\n\nMessages\n\ndef encPendingPreKeyXL67–71 ↗#PendingPreKey { optional uint32 pre_key_id = 1; bytes base_key = 2; int32 signed_pre_key_id = 3; uint64 timestamp = 4; }.\n\ndef encPendingKyberXL73–75 ↗#PendingKyberPreKey { uint32 pre_key_id = 1; bytes ciphertext = 2; }.\n\ndef encStateUnderExtrasL77–93 ↗#SessionStructure of a session-model state with extras x, fields in tag order 1–7, 9, 10, 11, 13, 14, 15. The pending items (9, 14) are written exactly while the session model's pendingPreKey flag is set.\n\ndef encodeRecordUnderExtrasL95–98 ↗#SessionRecord::serialize of a session-model state under extras E: RecordStructure { current_session = 1; } (no previous sessions).\n\ndef binStateOfUnderExtrasL100–106 ↗#The binary state of a session-model state under extras E: the party, the record bytes encodeRecordUnderExtras E g, and the epoch ghost EpochGhost.ofGhost g.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"LibsignalBinary/Specifications/LibsignalE2E/StateXModel.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.LibsignalE2E.StateXModel/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___LibsignalE2E___StateXModel"}});